{"slug":"Attacking_Guide","title":"Attacking Guide","section":"Guides","cats":[],"headings":[{"id":"Introduction","text":"Introduction","level":1},{"id":"Maximum_Population","text":"Maximum Population","level":1},{"id":"Population_Growth_Formula","text":"Population Growth Formula","level":1},{"id":"Population_Growth_Derivation","text":"Population Growth Derivation","level":1},{"id":"Troop_vs._Worker_Roles","text":"Troop vs. Worker Roles","level":2},{"id":"The_Shield_Icon_(Troop_Density_Indicator)","text":"The Shield Icon (Troop Density Indicator)","level":1},{"id":"How_Attacks_Work","text":"How Attacks Work","level":1},{"id":"Target_Selection","text":"Target Selection","level":2},{"id":"Combat_Resolution","text":"Combat Resolution","level":2},{"id":"Betrayal_Effect","text":"Betrayal Effect","level":2},{"id":"Defense_Posts","text":"Defense Posts","level":1},{"id":"Attack_Speed_(Processing_Rate)","text":"Attack Speed (Processing Rate)","level":1},{"id":"Tips","text":"Tips","level":1}],"html":"<table class=\"box-Update plainlinks metadata ambox ambox-content ambox-Update\" role=\"presentation\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"mbox-image\"><div class=\"mbox-image-div\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"/images/Red_clock.svg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-file-width=\"512\" data-file-height=\"512\"></span></span></div></td><td class=\"mbox-text\"><div class=\"mbox-text-span\">This article's factual accuracy may be compromised due to out-of-date information<b>.<span class=\"hide-when-compact\"> Please help update this article to reflect recent events or newly available information. <br><small>Last update: v23.0</small></span></b></div></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h1 id=\"Introduction\">Introduction</h1>\n<p>Attacking in OpenFront.io - A Complete Guide <em>(for version v23)</em></p>\n<h1 id=\"Maximum_Population\">Maximum Population</h1>\n<p>The maximum population in OpenFrontIO determines the upper limit of troops or resources a player can accumulate. It is influenced by several factors, including:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Number of Tiles Owned</strong>: The more tiles a player controls, the higher their maximum population.</li>\n<li><strong>City Levels</strong>: Higher-level cities contribute additional population capacity.</li>\n<li><strong>Game Difficulty</strong>: The difficulty setting modifies the maximum population for certain players (e.g., bots or “FakeHuman” players).</li>\n<li><strong>Player Type</strong>: Human players and bots have different scaling factors applied to their maximum population.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The formula for calculating the maximum population for human players (unless in “infinite troops” mode) is as follows:</p>\n<p><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle {\\text{maxPop}}=2\\cdot ({\\text{basePop}})+{\\text{cityBonus}}}}\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mtext>maxPop</mtext>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>2</mn>\n<mo>⋅</mo>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mtext>basePop</mtext>\n</mrow>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mtext>cityBonus</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n<annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle {\\text{maxPop}}=2\\cdot ({\\text{basePop}})+{\\text{cityBonus}}}}</annotation>\n</semantics>\n</math></span></span></p>\n<p>Where:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\textstyle {\\text{basePop}}={\\text{numTilesOwned}}^{0.6}\\cdot 1000+50000000}\"> <semantics> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mtext>basePop</mtext> </mrow> <mo>=</mo> <msup> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mtext>numTilesOwned</mtext> </mrow> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mn>0.6</mn> </mrow> </msup> <mo>⋅</mo> <mn>1000</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mn>50000000</mn> </mstyle> </mrow> <annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\textstyle {\\text{basePop}}={\\text{numTilesOwned}}^{0.6}\\cdot 1000+50000000}</annotation> </semantics> </math></span></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\textstyle {\\text{cityBonus}}={\\text{sumOfCityLevels}}\\cdot {\\text{cityPopulationIncrease}}}\"> <semantics> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mtext>cityBonus</mtext> </mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mtext>sumOfCityLevels</mtext> </mrow> <mo>⋅</mo> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mtext>cityPopulationIncrease</mtext> </mrow> </mstyle> </mrow> <annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\textstyle {\\text{cityBonus}}={\\text{sumOfCityLevels}}\\cdot {\\text{cityPopulationIncrease}}}</annotation> </semantics> </math></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Currently, <code>cityPopulationIncrease</code> is defined at 25,000, meaning that for each city added, an additional 25,000 troops is added to the maximum population capacity. This maximum population formula ensures that players who control more territory and build higher-level cities can sustain larger populations, encouraging strategic expansion and resource management.</p>\n<p>We can also see that players with minimum land and/or cities will still be provided some base value of capacity.</p>\n<h1 id=\"Population_Growth_Formula\">Population Growth Formula</h1>\n<p>In the game mechanics of OpenFrontIO, population growth is governed by a formula that balances the current population against the maximum population. This formula may change over time, but is currently defined in the <code>/src/core/configuration/DefaultConfig.ts</code> file in the OpenFrontIO repository ([<a href=\"https://github.com/openfrontio/OpenFrontIO\">|OpenFrontIO GitHub Repository</a>]).</p>\n<p>The population growth per tick is given by:</p>\n<p><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle {\\text{toAdd}}=\\left(10+{\\frac {{\\text{currentPopulation}}^{0.73}}{4}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(1-{\\frac {\\text{currentPopulation}}{\\text{maxPopulation}}}\\right)}}\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mtext>toAdd</mtext>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>10</mn>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mfrac>\n<msup>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mtext>currentPopulation</mtext>\n</mrow>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mn>0.73</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n<mo>⋅</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mo>−</mo>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mfrac>\n<mtext>currentPopulation</mtext>\n<mtext>maxPopulation</mtext>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n<annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle {\\text{toAdd}}=\\left(10+{\\frac {{\\text{currentPopulation}}^{0.73}}{4}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(1-{\\frac {\\text{currentPopulation}}{\\text{maxPopulation}}}\\right)}}</annotation>\n</semantics>\n</math></span></span></p>\n<p>Let:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle x={\\text{currentPopulation}}}}\"> <semantics> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"> <mi>x</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mtext>currentPopulation</mtext> </mrow> </mstyle> </mrow> </mstyle> </mrow> <annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle x={\\text{currentPopulation}}}}</annotation> </semantics> </math></span></span>,</li>\n<li><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle M={\\text{maxPopulation}}}}\"> <semantics> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"> <mi>M</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mtext>maxPopulation</mtext> </mrow> </mstyle> </mrow> </mstyle> </mrow> <annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle M={\\text{maxPopulation}}}}</annotation> </semantics> </math></span></span>,</li>\n<li><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle r={\\frac {x}{M}}}}\"> <semantics> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"> <mi>r</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mfrac> <mi>x</mi> <mi>M</mi> </mfrac> </mrow> </mstyle> </mrow> </mstyle> </mrow> <annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle r={\\frac {x}{M}}}}</annotation> </semantics> </math></span></span>, where <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle r}}\"> <semantics> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"> <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"> <mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"> <mi>r</mi> </mstyle> </mrow> </mstyle> </mrow> <annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle r}}</annotation> </semantics> </math></span></span> is the fraction of the maximum population.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Rewriting the formula in terms of <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle r}}\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mi>r</mi>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n<annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle r}}</annotation>\n</semantics>\n</math></span></span>, we have:</p>\n<p><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle f(r)=\\left(10+{\\frac {(M\\cdot r)^{0.73}}{4}}\\right)\\cdot (1-r)}}\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mi>f</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>10</mn>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mfrac>\n<mrow>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mi>M</mi>\n<mo>⋅</mo>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<msup>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mn>0.73</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n<mo>⋅</mo>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mo>−</mo>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n<annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle f(r)=\\left(10+{\\frac {(M\\cdot r)^{0.73}}{4}}\\right)\\cdot (1-r)}}</annotation>\n</semantics>\n</math></span></span></p>\n<p>This formula is optimized at roughly 42%. The full derivation is below.</p>\n<h1 id=\"Population_Growth_Derivation\">Population Growth Derivation</h1>\n<p>Our goal is to find the value of <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle r}}\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mi>r</mi>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n<annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle r}}</annotation>\n</semantics>\n</math></span></span> that maximizes <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle f(r)}}\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mi>f</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n<annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle f(r)}}</annotation>\n</semantics>\n</math></span></span>, which corresponds to the optimal fraction of the maximum population for maximum growth.</p>\n<p>Expanding <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle f(r)}}\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mi>f</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n<annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle f(r)}}</annotation>\n</semantics>\n</math></span></span>, we get:</p>\n<p><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle f(r)=\\left(10+{\\frac {M^{0.73}\\cdot r^{0.73}}{4}}\\right)\\cdot (1-r)}}\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mi>f</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>10</mn>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mfrac>\n<mrow>\n<msup>\n<mi>M</mi>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mn>0.73</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n<mo>⋅</mo>\n<msup>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mn>0.73</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n<mo>⋅</mo>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mo>−</mo>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n<annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle f(r)=\\left(10+{\\frac {M^{0.73}\\cdot r^{0.73}}{4}}\\right)\\cdot (1-r)}}</annotation>\n</semantics>\n</math></span></span></p>\n<p>Distribute <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle (1-r)}}\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mo>−</mo>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n<annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle (1-r)}}</annotation>\n</semantics>\n</math></span></span>:</p>\n<p><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle f(r)=10\\cdot (1-r)+{\\frac {M^{0.73}\\cdot r^{0.73}}{4}}\\cdot (1-r)}}\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mi>f</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>10</mn>\n<mo>⋅</mo>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mo>−</mo>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mfrac>\n<mrow>\n<msup>\n<mi>M</mi>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mn>0.73</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n<mo>⋅</mo>\n<msup>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mn>0.73</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n<mo>⋅</mo>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mo>−</mo>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n<annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle f(r)=10\\cdot (1-r)+{\\frac {M^{0.73}\\cdot r^{0.73}}{4}}\\cdot (1-r)}}</annotation>\n</semantics>\n</math></span></span></p>\n<p>Simplify further:</p>\n<p><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle f(r)=10-10r+{\\frac {M^{0.73}\\cdot r^{0.73}}{4}}-{\\frac {M^{0.73}\\cdot r^{1.73}}{4}}}}\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n<mi>f</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>10</mn>\n<mo>−</mo>\n<mn>10</mn>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mfrac>\n<mrow>\n<msup>\n<mi>M</mi>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mn>0.73</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n<mo>⋅</mo>\n<msup>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mn>0.73</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n<mo>−</mo>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mfrac>\n<mrow>\n<msup>\n<mi>M</mi>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mn>0.73</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n<mo>⋅</mo>\n<msup>\n<mi>r</mi>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n<mn>1.73</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n<annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle f(r)=10-10r+{\\frac {M^{0.73}\\cdot r^{0.73}}{4}}-{\\frac {M^{0.73}\\cdot r^{1.73}}{4}}}}</annotation>\n</semantics>\n</math></span></span></p>\n<p>To find the critical points, compute the derivative of <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle f(r)}}\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow class=\"MJX-TeX